proximate the weight of Stephanie's portion." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the weight of the cake Grant ate to the nearest hundred:\n\n$$\n745⟶700\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the weight of Grant's portion to the weight of Stephanie's portion is \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the weight of Grant's  part and the denominator represents  the weight of Stephanies part.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $700$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $100:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 100}{3\\times 100}=\\frac{700}{300}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Stephanie ate approximately $300$ grams of cake." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6c802e76-90be-5a83-ad3b-13ee92d8dca1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6c802e76-90be-5a83-ad3b-13ee92d8dca1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c802e76-90be-5a83-ad3b-13ee92d8dca1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-642d5471-d8d0-5f30-b841-f9ddb78ad020" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9bb2834b-2c4a-5de7-a43c-ec0d2aebeaa0" "answer-642d5471-d8d0-5f30-b841-f9ddb78ad020" "answer-3615741b-46a4-5227-b3d1-750afe938f70" "answer-60e762ea-1c99-5415-9c61-1cb6553b4b84" "answer-61007c72-a194-5bd7-9737-2ab6110d4866"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bb2834b-2c4a-5de7-a43c-ec0d2aebeaa0" :answer/id #uuid "9bb2834b-2c4a-5de7-a43c-ec0d2aebeaa0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$250$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-642d5471-d8d0-5f30-b841-f9ddb78ad020" :answer/id #uuid "642d5471-d8d0-5f30-b841-f9ddb78ad020" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$300$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3615741b-46a4-5227-b3d1-750afe938f70" :answer/id #uuid "3615741b-46a4-5227-b3d1-750afe938f70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$350$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60e762ea-1c99-5415-9c61-1cb6553b4b84" :answer/id #uuid "60e762ea-1c99-5415-9c61-1cb6553b4b84" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$400$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61007c72-a194-5bd7-9737-2ab6110d4866" :answer/id #uuid "61007c72-a194-5bd7-9737-2ab6110d4866" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$450$ grams" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-92ab7ff7-d02e-5687-bfb0-2e6e2beec2cb" :question/id #uuid "92ab7ff7-d02e-5687-bfb0-2e6e2beec2cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-364163" :question/problem "Maya and Leon get paid for painting houses. The ratio of Maya's reward to Leon's reward is $3:4.$ \nDuring a particular week, Leon received $$806.$ By rounding Leon's earnings to the nearest hundred, approximate the amount of money that Maya received." :question/worked-solution "First, let's approximate the amount of money that Leon received:\n\n$$\n$806⟶$800\n$$\n\nThe ratio of Maya's earnings to Leon's earnings is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents Maya's earnings  and the denominator represents Leon's earnings.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $800$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $200$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 200}{4\\times 200}=\\frac{600}{800}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Maya received approximately $$600.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0db908f9-7a3a-5a7e-a3ec-6a328a11d897"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0db908f9-7a3a-5a7e-a3ec-6a328a11d897" :answer-field/id #uuid "0db908f9-7a3a-5a7e-a3ec-6a328a11d897" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-45d235ac-7712-5ca4-877d-63407f23d444" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45d235ac-7712-5ca4-877d-63407f23d444" "answer-807be663-7835-5fd3-82ec-350b159ded0f" "answer-5b98ffd4-63ed-5add-bf98-ecf5d6492c8a" "answer-881d6191-65af-5d92-988e-e00ce240a7fa" "answer-3753fd0b-c081-5341-ae6b-6434522711ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45d235ac-7712-5ca4-877d-63407f23d444" :answer/id #uuid "45d235ac-7712-5ca4-877d-63407f23d444" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$600$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-807be663-7835-5fd3-82ec-350b159ded0f" :answer/id #uuid "807be663-7835-5fd3-82ec-350b159ded0f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$700$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b98ffd4-63ed-5add-bf98-ecf5d6492c8a" :answer/id #uuid "5b98ffd4-63ed-5add-bf98-ecf5d6492c8a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$760$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-881d6191-65af-5d92-988e-e00ce240a7fa" :answer/id #uuid "881d6191-65af-5d92-988e-e00ce240a7fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$840$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3753fd0b-c081-5341-ae6b-6434522711ce" :answer/id #uuid "3753fd0b-c081-5341-ae6b-6434522711ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$$900$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c4649cc4-2caa-54b1-a9d4-13acf6f413f0" :question/id #uuid "c4649cc4-2caa-54b1-a9d4-13acf6f413f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-364172" :question/problem "The number of laptops and tablets in store A is shown in the following table:\n\n| Laptops | Tablets |\n| --- | --- |\n| $72$ | $38$ |\n\nIn store B there are approximately $35$ laptops. The ratio of the number of laptops to the number of tablets in both stores is the same. By rounding the given data to the nearest ten, approximate the number of tablets in store B." :question/worked-solution "First, let's round the number of laptops and tablets in store A:\n\n- Laptops: $72⟶70$\n\n- Tablets: $38⟶40$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the number of laptops to the number of tablets (expressed as a fraction) is approximately:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70}{40}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of laptops and the denominator represents the number of tablets.\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $10$ gives an equivalent fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70÷10}{40÷10}=\\frac{7}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can make a numerator of $35$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 5}{4\\times 5}=\\frac{35}{20}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are approximately $20$ tablets in store B." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5db6ae51-1959-57ad-8dff-d3275311dd80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5db6ae51-1959-57ad-8dff-d3275311dd80" :answer-field/id #uuid "5db6ae51-1959-57ad-8dff-d3275311dd80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d704850-2838-563c-aef8-e418a2b3c148" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1a0f6ae-38cb-5459-b690-6d6809dc0a7d" "answer-022a4a93-f3c4-5aee-abd1-90bc3255912b" "answer-3d704850-2838-563c-aef8-e418a2b3c148" "answer-8e38cfb0-b6b5-576f-8f18-ac6fe927d170" "answer-c3f809e8-955b-5304-81e5-e3dc3285884c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1a0f6ae-38cb-5459-b690-6d6809dc0a7d" :answer/id #uuid "e1a0f6ae-38cb-5459-b690-6d6809dc0a7d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$15$ tablets" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-022a4a93-f3c4-5aee-abd1-90bc3255912b" :answer/id #uuid "022a4a93-f3c4-5aee-abd1-90bc3255912b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ tablets" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d704850-2838-563c-aef8-e418a2b3c148" :answer/id #uuid "3d704850-2838-563c-aef8-e418a2b3c148" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20$ tablets" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e38cfb0-b6b5-576f-8f18-ac6fe927d170" :answer/id #uuid "8e38cfb0-b6b5-576f-8f18-ac6fe927d170" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25$ tablets" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3f809e8-955b-5304-81e5-e3dc3285884c" :answer/id #uuid "c3f809e8-955b-5304-81e5-e3dc3285884c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$30$ tablets" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3d8d5793-d336-5605-bbdc-d6f9f23c2473" :activity/id #uuid "3d8d5793-d336-5605-bbdc-d6f9f23c2473" :activity/title "Approximating Ratios" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048840 :activity/course 17592186046669 :activity/steps ["step-16aae4ea-1ad8-5274-96f3-862ce4f5ef5f" "step-4ac6e817-f199-5922-9e9d-be3655e4c1c8" "step-69ee0c21-c1b2-583d-b271-f07238247567" "step-cba98600-887f-500a-b3d4-907fdab73e5e" "step-98230e05-80da-500f-9b67-ad4b98606748"] :activity/first-step "step-16aae4ea-1ad8-5274-96f3-862ce4f5ef5f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-16aae4ea-1ad8-5274-96f3-862ce4f5ef5f" :step/id #uuid "16aae4ea-1ad8-5274-96f3-862ce4f5ef5f" :step/content "question-4f394066-5fc4-5966-8c8c-7e49bac1b23a" :step/next "step-4ac6e817-f199-5922-9e9d-be3655e4c1c8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4ac6e817-f199-5922-9e9d-be3655e4c1c8" :step/id #uuid "4ac6e817-f199-5922-9e9d-be3655e4c1c8" :step/content "question-132a5e4f-2931-5c22-94d5-e6d628c0a5d8" :step/next "step-69ee0c21-c1b2-583d-b271-f07238247567" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-69ee0c21-c1b2-583d-b271-f07238247567" :step/id #uuid "69ee0c21-c1b2-583d-b271-f07238247567" :step/content "question-9587827d-60b3-5a55-a4d3-895d1d528b37" :step/next "step-cba98600-887f-500a-b3d4-907fdab73e5e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cba98600-887f-500a-b3d4-907fdab73e5e" :step/id #uuid "cba98600-887f-500a-b3d4-907fdab73e5e" :step/content "question-92ab7ff7-d02e-5687-bfb0-2e6e2beec2cb" :step/next "step-98230e05-80da-500f-9b67-ad4b98606748" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-98230e05-80da-500f-9b67-ad4b98606748" :step/id #uuid "98230e05-80da-500f-9b67-ad4b98606748" :step/content "question-c4649cc4-2caa-54b1-a9d4-13acf6f413f0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157352 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1ac28018-b80f-5b5b-b911-ee1b1c7f7b2a" "question-3927d759-d3f3-597c-93a6-57d23bec620b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157167 :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x= \\dfrac{1}{2}y - \\sqrt y\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0-\\sqrt{0}=0 \\\\ y=1 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1-\\sqrt{1}=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y=4 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4-\\sqrt{4}=0 \\\\ y=16 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16-\\sqrt{16}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\dfrac12$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(0,0), \\quad \\left(-\\dfrac 12,1\\right), \\quad (0,4), \\quad (4,16).\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/70/709bfcd1e69a0e4fd88d95fb9d8592de93921fad230b5f892059525871dc50fb.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157353 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8d551751-5afc-56a3-aafa-744ff6b13a09" "question-12f6ec39-cedb-58cb-b548-33c88831eff2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157168 :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Sketch  the graph of $x=f(y).$\n\n![](images/76/76268e0ba23b56af4c7215a4a44f459e6a3ea42454f53df1d39894df16513865.png)" :question/worked-solution "To plot the graph of $x=f(y),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and reflect it over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/2e/2e11bec1e27fd59a1b4ea4e44070591acf5cd8fefebe6d5e1a46ef0be3f5129f.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157354 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d0398ee6-00a7-50a0-8e21-d6ea37fa1ef7" "question-901a0148-bd15-5ce7-9470-9a379d5bfbe0" "question-a12fcacc-90b5-5cdd-9ea9-725215f67451" "question-580eb058-5204-5604-8964-e7eb4b3f475e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157169 :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x=-2y^2 - 3y.$" :question/worked-solution "To plot $x=-2y^2-3y,$ we will first plot the function $y=-2x^2-3x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x.$\n\nThe curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny = -x(2x+3)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we see that we have a negative parabola with roots at $x=0$ and $x=-\\dfrac32.$ Therefore, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/c2/c2a1492655ff33a49bd21e911b13b99d67191a4cd39683f34fca4be295dda41a.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=-2y^2-3y,$ we just have to reflect the curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/7f/7fbfb3fd5bbacbf1c974bf654e993a7203934db5d679bfaa89ddc0c54e39a7df.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-1ac28018-b80f-5b5b-b911-ee1b1c7f7b2a" :question/id #uuid "1ac28018-b80f-5b5b-b911-ee1b1c7f7b2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-88494" :question/problem "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{y}+8}{{y}^{3/2}}\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |" :question/worked-solution "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=1 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{1}+8}{{1}^{3/2}}=10 \\\\ y=4 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{4}+8}{{4}^{3/2}}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ y=9 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{9}+8}{{9}^{3/2}}=\\frac{14}{27} \\\\ y=16 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{2\\sqrt{16}+8}{{16}^{3/2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $10$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ | $\\frac{14}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(10,1),\\,(\\frac{3}{2},4),\\,(\\frac{14}{27},9),\\,(\\frac{1}{4},16).\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/56/56b5c0ad101bb2d26a66fa84accdd11c629f150f64892aad4c20194d647428e8.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-181bb570-f32f-54c7-b66f-e128230f4894"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-181bb570-f32f-54c7-b66f-e128230f4894" :answer-field/id #uuid "181bb570-f32f-54c7-b66f-e128230f4894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e89729f-4aa5-5f8e-8605-af38cb4a0a32" :answer-field/choices ["answer-140f0441-ab22-51c0-bb54-548d036f79bf" "answer-9e89729f-4aa5-5f8e-8605-af38cb4a0a32" "answer-413468bb-bf43-520f-a959-6820c131332a" "answer-b47aa2c4-bf24-540e-b2c6-e71ad2103386" "answer-3b4af678-eebf-5129-a4dc-f2c1f159f21a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-140f0441-ab22-51c0-bb54-548d036f79bf" :answer/id #uuid "140f0441-ab22-51c0-bb54-548d036f79bf" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/0d/0d73296f544fe38cdd7b7c671f0d562dc014c0821a09c17b8c5d43f8b532c56d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e89729f-4aa5-5f8e-8605-af38cb4a0a32" :answer/id #uuid "9e89729f-4aa5-5f8e-8605-af38cb4a0a32" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/44/44b075fb9d20591a979e3a3ca175e7081cf72e6b6614419f5c7170ea119b4d7f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-413468bb-bf43-520f-a959-6820c131332a" :answer/id #uuid "413468bb-bf43-520f-a959-6820c131332a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7b/7b6dcce471b929ddda958bed2d5d5a35e57290c2ca95281491656bf81c567cca.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b47aa2c4-bf24-540e-b2c6-e71ad2103386" :answer/id #uuid "b47aa2c4-bf24-540e-b2c6-e71ad2103386" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d6/d6cd49cd9f696918d913b7486312d8f9c495cde965ab9e5487278c516e0f0cb6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b4af678-eebf-5129-a4dc-f2c1f159f21a" :answer/id #uuid "3b4af678-eebf-5129-a4dc-f2c1f159f21a" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/e9/e941fbe5ea73fa41edebc159f723f2ad3cb2b461fc590733aa1cb8de15b7034d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3927d759-d3f3-597c-93a6-57d23bec620b" :question/id #uuid "3927d759-d3f3-597c-93a6-57d23bec620b" :question/math-academy-id "q-88516" :question/problem "Determine which of the following is the graph of $x=(2y+1)^{2}-6\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |" :question/worked-solution "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-\\frac{1}{2} & \\,⟶\\,x={[2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+1]}^{2}-6=-6 \\\\ y=0 & \\,⟶\\,x=(2\\cdot 0+1)^{2}-6=-5 \\\\ y=1 & \\,⟶\\,x=(2\\cdot 1+1)^{2}-6=3 \\\\ y=\\frac{3}{2} & \\,⟶\\,x={[2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})+1]}^{2}-6=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $\\frac{3}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $3$ | $10$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(-6,-\\frac{1}{2}),\\,(-5,0),\\,(3,1),\\,(10,\\frac{3}{2}).\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/de/ded8b752a5acdd94b4e73a4cf7b301ed0d616b0cfd35896b5c9e5275fc8ca2ad.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c76bdfa1-89f9-5bce-8d5d-17b75468935a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c76bdfa1-89f9-5bce-8d5d-17b75468935a" :answer-field/id #uuid "c76bdfa1-89f9-5bce-8d5d-17b75468935a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-86c8eedc-e3db-5bb4-a1cc-6df762823b30" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86c8eedc-e3db-5bb4-a1cc-6df762823b30" "answer-cd083a00-a54b-57a1-a7ab-de2582e682fa" "answer-45ac3456-b50c-58a3-9d24-81a805df53de" "answer-b919