4958524debe28fa10c1165e3243f2a70c0461d2e458908f2a2.png)\n\nLet $T=\\{-2,-1,0,1,2\\}.$ The graph above shows the value of $g(x)$ for each $x\\in T.$ Assuming that all the dots have integer coordinates, compute the following:\n\n${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-3}}\n\n$\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nFrom the graph, \n\n- the highest point is at $(-1,2),$ so ${max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=2$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-1,$ and\n\n- the lowest point is at $(1,-4),$ so ${min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=-4$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in T}g(x)=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84ab0f43-dce5-5b24-af34-9e9667e2f676" "answer-field-4c188041-f98d-5213-a554-d3bd72acb99d" "answer-field-b0c91b01-5a9e-53cd-bf12-66fe6e064a64" "answer-field-6148f234-5233-586e-8e8b-314aa1cd285e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84ab0f43-dce5-5b24-af34-9e9667e2f676" :answer-field/id #uuid "84ab0f43-dce5-5b24-af34-9e9667e2f676" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7ab5858b-e187-54e0-9289-2591e78bae5e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ab5858b-e187-54e0-9289-2591e78bae5e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ab5858b-e187-54e0-9289-2591e78bae5e" :answer/id #uuid "7ab5858b-e187-54e0-9289-2591e78bae5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4c188041-f98d-5213-a554-d3bd72acb99d" :ans